// A comment line past the column limit: cut at its last space that fits, the cut words joining the
// paragraph's next line; a caution, a table row, a list item, a long address, a trailing comment
// and a line of wide characters within its columns are left as written.
const src_comment_cut_in: U8[] =
    """//< Comments that cross the column limit, cut at the last space that fits
//<
//< This detail paragraph has one line that runs far past the hundredth column because a name in it grew.
//< The next line of the same paragraph takes the carried words at its start.
//< This line runs past the limit too, and the line below it is a caution, so its words stand alone here.
//< Caution: a caution opens a paragraph of its own and takes no words carried from above it.
// | a | table row far too wide for one hundred columns of text keeps its cells exactly as written by hand |
// - a list item far too wide for one hundred columns of text keeps its own line exactly as it was written by hand
// https://example.com/a/very/long/address/that/is/one/word/and/wider/than/the/column/limit/itself/x/y/z/w
// 漢字かな漢字かな漢字かな漢字かな漢字かな漢字かな漢字かな漢字かな漢字かな漢字かな
// 漢字かな漢字 漢字かな漢字 漢字かな漢字 漢字かな漢字 漢字かな漢字 漢字かな漢字 漢字かな漢字 漢字かな漢字 漢字かな漢字
fn main(): I32
    // An ordinary comment in a body whose one line is far too long for the formatter's column limit.
    x: = 1 // a trailing comment stays as it is even where its line grows well past one hundred columns
    return x
"""

